course: dictionary
lesson: 13248
title: Words about places and people
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Ghanaian is an adjective that tells you something comes from Ghana, a country in West Africa. «She cooked a Ghanaian dish of jollof rice for the class.» The word dish and the name of the food are clues. Ghanaian tells you where the food comes from.
explain: Ghanaian can also name a person. «My friend Kofi is Ghanaian, and his family moved to London.» Here Ghanaian means a person from Ghana, just as British means a person from Britain. To check, swap in «from Ghana» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Ghanaian always has a capital G, because it names a country or its people. «Ghanaian culture» means the music, food, clothes and customs of Ghana. A phrase like «a Ghanaian-British family» shows a family with links to both Ghana and Britain.
fact: Ghanaian means from or to do with Ghana, a country in West Africa.
fact: A Ghanaian is a person from Ghana. The plural is Ghanaians.
fact: Accra is the capital city of Ghana.
fact: Ghana was the first country in sub-Saharan Africa to break free from colonial rule, in 1957.
fact: Kente cloth, jollof rice and highlife music are all part of Ghanaian culture.
exercise: «The class tasted Ghanaian jollof rice at the school fair.» What does Ghanaian tell you about the rice? | It is made only with fruit | It comes from Japan | It is always cold | *It comes from Ghana
exercise: «Mrs Mensah is a Ghanaian who moved to Canada.» Which word in the sentence names a person from Ghana? | Mrs | moved | *Ghanaian | Canada
exercise: What is the capital city of Ghana? | *Accra | Nairobi | Lagos | Kumasi
test: «Kofi's family is Ghanaian-British.» What does the Ghanaian part tell you? | They live in a castle | They dislike music | They are all very tall | *They have links to Ghana
test: In which year did Ghana gain independence from colonial rule? | 1975 | 1907 | 1857 | *1957
exam: Which sentence uses Ghanaian to mean a person? | *«My neighbour is a Ghanaian.» | «The Ghanaian food was spicy.» | «Ghanaian culture is rich and colourful.»
